{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"15c21fdd49b2434c26978157a4cd428cc3d0f54d7355ac822bd61b181a7150d2","packTokens":3664,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":240,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1450,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1652,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees can sign in using their Folio3 Google account, with employee profiles and vehicle details populated or registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can release today's parking with a single action and view its status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Dedicated parking holders can schedule or cancel parking releases up to 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Employees without dedicated parking can view availability and claim released parking on a first-come, first-served basis.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Use license plate recognition to verify temporary parking authorizations at the entrance and record attempts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Track parking utilization and generate and email weekly reports to designated stakeholders.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What may Parking Administrators and Security Guards do in the web app, beyond the functions already described?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Administrators manage employee and parking records, assignments, configuration, and report recipients; guards use only the entrance indicator and existing sticker process.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may receive reports that identify employees and their unused parking, and how are recipients maintained?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Parking Administrator maintains a named recipient list; only those recipients receive the report.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"Which source is authoritative for employee profiles, dedicated-parking assignments, and registered vehicles when an employee signs in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the corporate directory for employee details and an administrator-maintained parking assignment and vehicle list.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"For an employee with multiple registered vehicles, what counts as parking utilization when any one of their plates is detected entering that day?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Count the allocation as used if any vehicle registered to that employee is detected.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"How long should parking-release audit history, LPR verification attempts, and utilization events be retained?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply Folio3's existing records-retention policy to these records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"What makes an employee without dedicated parking eligible to claim a released space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Any active Folio3 employee without a dedicated assignment who has at least one registered vehicle may claim.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"Can a temporary parking user cancel a claim after successfully claiming a space?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Claims cannot be cancelled by the user once confirmed.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"If a dedicated holder's released space has been claimed but the holder's permanently stickered vehicle arrives, how should the system treat the temporary claimant's authorization?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep the temporary authorization valid; the stickered vehicle continues through the existing process even if this exceeds configured capacity.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Approve all 24 requirements as one run.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"Should all 24 requirements proceed as one implementation run, or should scope be reduced for this run?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Require the request to be authenticated as coming from trusted Folio3 LPR equipment.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"How must an LPR verification request prove it comes from trusted Folio3 equipment before it can activate the entrance indicator?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Only Parking Administrators may view and export utilization records; deny access to all other roles.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may view employee utilization records and export them as CSV?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Do not complete administrator setup until deployment configuration supplies a designated active Folio3 account; grant that account the initial Parking Administrator role.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"question\": \"What should deployment do if no designated active Folio3 bootstrap account is supplied?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Explicitly set the green indicator inactive on every verification failure.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"question\": \"When verification fails while the green indicator may already be active, what should the system do with the indicator?\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The application will be available on both iOS and Android platforms.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-17\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Build the Folio3 Parking product as a responsive web app for phone, tablet, and desktop, with touch-sized controls on narrow screens.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-14\",\n  \"question\": \"May the weekly report email contain employee-identifying utilization data for named recipients who are not Parking Administrators?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Send employee-identifying reports only to configured recipients who are Parking Administrators; omit other listed addresses from delivery.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-15\",\n  \"question\": \"What validation must succeed before a Google OAuth callback can create an authenticated session?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Validate the Google-issued ID token signature, issuer, and audience; verify OAuth state; and confirm the account is an active Folio3 employee.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-16\",\n  \"question\": \"What replay defense should authenticated LPR entrance-verification requests use?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require a unique authenticated request ID or nonce and reject any ID or nonce already accepted.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"1. Require Google OAuth callbacks to validate the ID token signature, issuer, and audience, verify OAuth state, and confirm the account belongs to an active Folio3 employee before creating an authenticated session; reject personal Gmail, non-Folio3, inactive, or invalid requests without a session.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"2. Return authenticated employees’ profiles with corporate-directory details and any administrator-maintained parking assignment, floor, and registered-vehicle records, and prevent non-administrators from viewing another employee’s profile.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"3. Require employees without a registered vehicle to register at least one license plate before releasing or claiming parking, and allow vehicle records to include optional make, model, and color.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"4. Give Parking Administrators read-only access to corporate-directory details and allow them to create, view, and update linked employee parking assignments and vehicle records without changing directory details; deny these changes to other roles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"5. Keep initial administrator setup blocked until deployment configuration designates an active Folio3 account, then grant it the initial Parking Administrator role; allow Parking Administrators to configure release time, floor capacities, the work calendar, named report recipients, and administrator and Security Guard role assignments.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"6. Render every employee and administrator page responsively for phone, tablet, and desktop widths, without horizontal overflow and with touch-sized primary controls on narrow viewports.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"7. Let dedicated parking holders release today’s reserved parking in one action, recording exactly one release and showing its status as Released.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"8. Show dedicated assignments as Reserved by default on configured working days, and make a same-day release claimable at the configured daily release time if submitted earlier, or immediately if submitted later, using the Folio3 office time zone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"9. Let dedicated holders schedule releases for one or more dates up to 30 days ahead, make each claimable at the daily release time on its selected date, and show scheduled dates and statuses in the release calendar; reject dates more than 30 days ahead.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"10. Let holders cancel unclaimed scheduled releases, but reject cancellation after a release has been claimed and preserve the claim.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"11. Show claimable released parking and the current available-space count to active Folio3 employees with no dedicated assignment and at least one registered vehicle; reject ineligible availability requests or claims without creating claims.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"12. Assign each released allocation to only the earliest accepted eligible claim, return its configured floor, and prevent claimants from cancelling confirmed temporary claims.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"13. Email eligible employees without dedicated parking who have a registered vehicle when a released allocation becomes claimable, using the configured fixed template.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"14. Leave the existing process for permanently stickered vehicles unaffected and preserve any temporary claim already made for that date, including when configured capacity is exceeded.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"15. Authenticate entrance-verification requests as originating from trusted Folio3 LPR equipment, require a unique authenticated request ID or nonce, reject previously accepted IDs or nonces, and verify readable detected-car plates against that date’s temporary authorizations; activate the green indicator only for valid authorizations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"16. On failed entrance verification, deny entry through the temporary-parking process, issue an explicit command to set the green indicator inactive, and record any error if that integration is unavailable; return no authorization response and make no activation call for non-car detections.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"17. Record every successful and unsuccessful entrance verification with its timestamp, readable plate or empty plate field, result, and entry status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"18. Record daily utilization from registered-vehicle entry records, counting an allocation as used when any vehicle registered to its employee is detected that day, and record unused dedicated and temporary parking as specified.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"19. Generate a weekly report on Monday morning in the Folio3 office time zone for the preceding Monday-through-Sunday week, including unused dedicated and temporary parking, daily and weekly utilization statistics, released-space and claim totals, and utilization percentage calculated as used eligible allocations divided by eligible allocations, or zero when there are none.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"20. Send weekly employee-identifying report emails only to configured report recipients who have the Parking Administrator role; omit other listed and unconfigured addresses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"21. Allow only Parking Administrators to view filterable utilization records and export the displayed records as CSV; deny both operations to callers in every other role.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"22. Retain parking-release audit history, LPR verification attempts, and utilization events according to Folio3’s existing records-retention policy.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"23. Limit Phase 1 utilization functionality to monitoring, recording, and reporting, without creating automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}